          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "saip",
          "text": "Colorado Car Insurance Laws",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bais",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sair",
          "text": "Colorado is a fault-based car insurance state. This is the most common type of insurance law in the U.S. It states that the person or party at fault for causing a car crash will be financially responsible for medical bills, property repairs and other losses that arise as a result of the collision. In a state that abides by a no-fault rule, on the other hand, all parties seek benefits from their own insurance providers, regardless of fault for the accident.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "baiu",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sait",
          "text": "Colorado’s car insurance law gives you the right to file a personal injury lawsuit against the driver or party that caused your car accident. A lawsuit could result in greater financial compensation than an insurance claim, such as an award given to you for pain and suffering. In contrast, a no-fault law would only give you the right to file a lawsuit if your injuries meet a threshold, such as an injury that is permanently disabling.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "baiw",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "saiv",
          "text": "The drawback to Colorado’s fault system, however, is that you or your car accident attorney will need to prove fault before you can recover compensation under Colorado’s fault law, whereas in a no-fault state, fault is irrelevant and not necessary to prove for financial benefits.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "baiy",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "saix",
